<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / SYSTEM INSTALLATION</p>
    <h1>xchroot</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Enter a Vylen installation target with the filesystems and DNS context
        required for package administration.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># xchroot &lt;chroot-dir&gt; [command]</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>xchroot /mnt
xchroot /mnt portsync
xchroot /mnt emerald sysup -y
xchroot /mnt /bin/bash</code></pre>

    <p>
        The helper mounts <code>/dev</code>, <code>/dev/pts</code>,
        <code>/dev/shm</code>, <code>/proc</code>, <code>/run</code>,
        <code>/sys</code>, optional EFI variables, <code>/tmp</code>, and the
        host resolver. It cleans those mounts on exit and preserves command
        argument boundaries.
    </p>
</section>
